senses.gloss:
miśraka, nt.,
(1) a kind of literary composition, acc. to Tib. spel ma, a mixture of prose and verse (cf. Skt. miśra, -ka): Mvy 〔1456〕; the surrounding terms denote kinds of commentaries, paddhati and ṭīkā;
(2) (= Pali missaka, nt.), n. of a pleasure-grove of the gods, presumably = next: ˚ke, loc. sg., LV 〔45.5〕 (vs).
